%S A400905 3,0,3,1,4,5,4,6,1,5,9,1,4,3,3,0,9,2,4,2,9,9,3,1,7,1,2,9,9,6,0
%N A400905 Decimal expansion of the Flint Hills series: Sum_{n > 0} 1/(n^3 * sin(n)^2).
%C A400905 This series converges if the irrationality exponent of Pi is less than 2.5 (Alekseyev) and its convergence implies that the irrationality exponent of Pi is less than or equal to 2.5 (Meiburg). OpenAI released a preprint indicating that the irrationality exponent is 2 and hence the series converges.
%D A400905 C. A. Pickover, The Mathematics of Oz: Mental Gymnastics from Beyond the Edge, Cambridge Univ. Press, 2002, pp. 57-59 and 265-268.
%H A400905 Max A. Alekseyev, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1104.5100">On Convergence of the Flint Hills Series</a>, arXiv:1104.5100 [math.CA], 2011.
%H A400905 Alex Meiburg, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.13356">Bounds on Irrationality Measures and the Flint-Hills Series</a>, arXiv:2208.13356 [math.NT], 2022.
%H A400905 OpenAI, <a href="https://github.com/openai/math/tree/main/preprints/The-irrationality-exponent-of-pi-is-2-September-24-2026">The irrationality exponent of Pi is 2</a> (2026).
%H A400905 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/FlintHillsSeries.html">Flint Hills Series</a>.
%e A400905 30.3145461591433092429931712996...
%Y A400905 Cf. A002485, A046947, A002117.
